+	(47: wheeled 4x4s, pickups, van, trucks, APCs, IFVs, tanks, anti-air, artillery). Schema: VehicleBodies/Types.luau;
+	budgets and the kill switch: VehicleBodies/init.luau; the lane guide: api.md.
+	One part per line (tools/BuyPathStatic.py counts them: a Mirror part counts 2, at most 40 per vehicle). No Neon floods:
+	the only glow is the Railgun Carrier's two small emissive rail tips (VehicleBodies.Budget MaxEmissive 2).
+	Every drawn part except the see-through glass is Hit = true: shots and rays hit the body the player sees.
+	A rider who may shoot from his seat (VehicleCombatConfig.SeatFire: the 4x4s, cars and trucks) keeps his head behind
+	glass or in the open (less than half of the lines out of his head end on the body); a seat the body closes in (the
+	Troop Transport's covered bed, the Armored Truck's armoured cab) is enclosed by VehicleCombatConfig.SeatFire
+	.EnclosedSeats (shielded, no firing out), whichever body is drawn.
+	Body-local studs: Y up from the ground line (the tyre / track bottoms), nose at -Z, X = 0 / Z = 0 under the kit chassis
+	(the physics pivot). Every family is drawn at Scale 1 in real studs next to the 5.2-stud avatar; a vehicle's Scale
+	grows or shrinks the whole body (its seat heights are re-worked per vehicle so the rider stays in the hatch / cab).
+
+	Where the rider sits (seat TOP; a seated R15: hips +0.5, shoulders +2.6, head top +3.7, feet 1.0 below / 1.45 ahead):
+	  4x4 / quad / buggy: low in an open seat, the tub side to the waist, windscreen and roll bar round him.
+	  car / pickup / van / trucks / MRAP: in a closed cab, hips and legs in the solid lower shell, head and shoulders
+	    behind the side glass under the roof (the head top at least 0.05 under it).
+	  APC / IFV / tank / anti-air / artillery: in a hatch, the hull or turret roof at his chest (head and shoulders out),
+	    his legs inside the hull. A tracked kit drives at x = 0 (it is not in Drive.Stability.DriveAtComXFamilies), so
+	    every tracked body seats its DriverSeat on the centre line: a solo driver's weight never turns it (G7).
+	Every seat stays inside the kit's collidable box (VehicleBodies.SeatKitInset), so the kit's hidden seats, exits,
+	Ride and the physics are the kit's own; a store body (VisualAssetConfig.Vehicles) still wins when it loads, and
+	these bodies are then only its fallback (LUV 4x4 family, Quad / Buggy, van, pickups, APC family, trucks).
