+# blueprint. G2 inside a family every two bodies differ, seen from the side AND from behind, by at least 8 studs^2 of
+# shape or of colour (RGB distance >= 40), at Scale 1 (the chase camera zooms with size). G3 every body's visible half
+# length (the symmetric box the spawn chooser clears, WE_VisualHalfLength) <= 14.4 so a spawn at the home pad centre
+# clears the Garage sign 14.6 behind it, half width <= 6.5. G4 every drawn part is what a shot hits (Hit = true) except
+# see-through glass. G5 the nameplate / HP bar (LabelHeight, or the builder's rule) is over every seated head. G6 the
+# framework hunks this lane needs: the Hit flag + step 4c (VehicleBodyBuilder, Types). G7 a vehicle whose kit family's
+# drive force pushes at x = 0 (not in DriveAtComXFamilies / DriveAtComXPartBodyFamilies: every tracked kit) seats its
+# DriverSeat on the centre line (|x| <= 0.05): an off-centre solo driver would turn it (vsr_phys_r23 YAW). G8 a rider who
+# may shoot from his seat (VehicleCombatConfig.SeatFire.OpenFamilies, not in SeatFire.EnclosedSeats) is as open as he
+# shoots: fewer than half of 72 lines out of his head (24 bearings x -8 / 0 / +8 degrees, 12 studs) end on an opaque Hit
+# part of his own body; every EnclosedSeats name is a seat of that vehicle's body. Fix 2 (review round 2):
+# G9 SPLASH: VehicleHealth measures a blast to the nearest drawn Hit part (CanQuery parts of WE_PartBody) or the kit
+#    Chassis box, only for a class listed in VehicleCombatConfig.Splash.PartBodyHits (Ground) and only on a model that
+#    carries WE_PartBody; the fix-1 symmetric visual box (Splash.VisualBox, WE_VisualHalfLength / Width / Top) is gone.
+# G10 KILL SWITCH: the truck / APC drive point follows the centre of mass only with the Part body on
+#    (DriveAtComXPartBodyFamilies + the WE_PartBody test in VehicleService._Ballast; DriveAtComXFamilies stays R2.3's
